+// the raw view over that. Measured need: the first retail slot-70 call names VA 0x1f6f8400220, which no buffer of the
+// layer holds (slot 133's one placed resource is at 0x1f6f8f00000). The copy happens when the view is made, so a write
+// the title does after this call is not seen: import (VK_KHR_external_memory_win32) is the real fix, this is the proof
+// that the bytes reach the GPU at all. One buffer per call, never released (a boot-level diagnostic).
+ID3D12Resource* acquire_console_va_buffer(DeviceProxy* self, std::uint64_t va, std::uint64_t bytes) {
+    // The measured first call's width is 174 MiB (the title's 0xAE00000-byte buffers), so the cap has to sit above
+    // that; it only bounds a copy that would be absurd for this diagnostic path.
